"answer": "The Q2 budget revisions involve several key updates and impacts. Diana Wells (Chief Auditor) notes that financial records, particularly those related to recent budget revisions, must be accurate and available for the upcoming Q2 audit. Oliver Grant (Project Manager) reports that capital expenditure projects for Q2 came in 10% over budget, necessitating a reallocation of funds and adjustments to financial projections. Henry Scott (CEO) indicates that Jordan, as finance manager, will need to outline the impact of these budget revisions during the Q2 earnings call. Finally, Karen Smith (CFO) confirms that the Q2 budget has been adjusted, with funds shifted toward emerging market bonds, resulting in a revised profit forecast of $9.378 million, a 3.5% increase from previous estimates."
